IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cyp-protection`

-- Children and Young Persons Act 1993, ss 2, 5 to 8 -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case or subsidiary legislation (none was retrieved).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_cyp.py). Expected results were written by
-- hand from the text.

§ `Fixtures`

`a parent who beat the child` MEANS Carer WITH
    `has custody, charge or care` IS TRUE
    `ill-treated the child` IS TRUE
    `knew or had reason to believe of the risk from another` IS FALSE
    `took reasonable steps to protect` IS FALSE

`a parent who knew the partner was violent and did nothing` MEANS Carer WITH
    `has custody, charge or care` IS TRUE
    `ill-treated the child` IS FALSE
    `knew or had reason to believe of the risk from another` IS TRUE
    `took reasonable steps to protect` IS FALSE

`a parent who knew and moved out with the child` MEANS Carer WITH
    `has custody, charge or care` IS TRUE
    `ill-treated the child` IS FALSE
    `knew or had reason to believe of the risk from another` IS TRUE
    `took reasonable steps to protect` IS TRUE

`a neighbour who knew` MEANS Carer WITH
    `has custody, charge or care` IS FALSE
    `ill-treated the child` IS FALSE
    `knew or had reason to believe of the risk from another` IS TRUE
    `took reasonable steps to protect` IS FALSE

§ `s 2`

#ASSERT `the person's status under the Act` 13 EQUALS "child"
#ASSERT `the person's status under the Act` 14 EQUALS "young person"
#ASSERT `the person's status under the Act` 17 EQUALS "young person"
#ASSERT `the person's status under the Act` 18 EQUALS "adult"

§ `s 5`

#ASSERT `the child is in need of care or protection` `no parent or guardian`
#ASSERT `the child is in need of care or protection` `abandoned and parent cannot be found`
#ASSERT `the child is in need of care or protection` `parent neglects necessities`
#ASSERT `the child is in need of care or protection` `ill-treated by parent`
#ASSERT `the child is in need of care or protection` `at risk from another and parent will not protect`
#ASSERT `the child is in need of care or protection` `parent refuses needed medical treatment`
#ASSERT `the child is in need of care or protection` `confined in a small space as discipline`
#ASSERT `the child is in need of care or protection` `exposed to violence against a related person`
#ASSERT `the child is in need of care or protection` `found begging`
#ASSERT NOT `the child is in need of care or protection` `parents divorcing`
#ASSERT NOT `the child is in need of care or protection` `strict but loving parent`

§ `s 6`

#ASSERT `the carer commits a section 6 offence` `a parent who beat the child`
#ASSERT `the carer commits a section 6 offence` `a parent who knew the partner was violent and did nothing`
#ASSERT NOT `the carer commits a section 6 offence` `a parent who knew and moved out with the child`
#ASSERT NOT `the carer commits a section 6 offence` `a neighbour who knew`

#ASSERT `the maximum imprisonment in years for ill-treatment` TRUE EQUALS 14
#ASSERT `the maximum imprisonment in years for ill-treatment` FALSE EQUALS 8

§ `s 7`

#ASSERT `the carer is taken to have allowed it for begging` TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the carer is taken to have allowed it for begging` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the carer is taken to have allowed it for begging` FALSE FALSE TRUE

§ `s 8`

#ASSERT `exploitation is presumed` `step-parent`
#ASSERT `exploitation is presumed` `teacher at their school`
#ASSERT `exploitation is presumed` `their music teacher`
#ASSERT `exploitation is presumed` `their doctor`
#ASSERT `exploitation is presumed` `their lawyer`
#ASSERT NOT `exploitation is presumed` `spouse`
#ASSERT NOT `exploitation is presumed` `a peer`

